  "worked_solution": "A function $h(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nh(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}h(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $h(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}h(x,y,z)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(tx,ty,tz) & =(tx)^{3}(ty)+(tx)(ty)^{3}-8(tz)^{3} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}{x}^{3}y+{t}^{4}x{y}^{3}-8{t}^{3}{z}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's impossible to write this as\n\n$$\n{t}^{n}h(x,y,z)={t}^{n}({x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}-8{z}^{3})\n$$\n\nand so $h(x,y,z)$ is not homogeneous.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
